ld" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "nonlinear"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037933/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f523ef0a0a7c999fb3fb80b5c4e505e3facc7db57aa15757d4c111808136a0e" "basis" 1953 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-337739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following differential operator:\n\n$$\nD(y)={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+y\n$$\n\nFill in the steps in the reasoning below.\n\nFor any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={{field-2}}+{{field-3}} \\\\  & +ab\\cdot {{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+b{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since {{field-5}} \nthe operator $D$ is {{field-6}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037933/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f523ef0a0a7c999fb3fb80b5c4e505e3facc7db57aa15757d4c111808136a0e" "basis" 1953 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-337739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aL({y}_{1})+bL({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}))}^{2}+(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={(a\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+2ab\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2} \\\\  & +a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{b}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2} \\\\  & +ab\\cdot (2\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is *not* the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a[{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{y}_{1}]+b[{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+b{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}),$ the operator $D$ is $\\text{nonlinear}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037933/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f523ef0a0a7c999fb3fb80b5c4e505e3facc7db57aa15757d4c111808136a0e" "basis" 1953 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-337739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "daa03b1e971a9bd14d6e1de601a82dccaeff80b6a805a0c9d410d350f02ff85d" "basis" 1953 "verification" "/hom