eveloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-337728" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-337728" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-337728" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "linear"] ["text" "nonlinear"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-337728" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "nonlinear"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-130256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\n- ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{2}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{3}(y)={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-130256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nLet's check each case in turn.\n\n- The first operator is **not** linear. To see why, we first evaluate the left-hand side of the linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{1}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+ab({y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{D}_{1}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{1}({y}_{2}) & =a[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operator is indeed linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{2}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{2}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{2}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operator is also linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{3}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2ax\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+2bx\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =a[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}]+b[{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2x\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{3}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{3}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-130256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f02d4e05e1514d523792d5d9e48497a88d0a14a3d5392cc77fed0b9f3315f7"} {"question" "q-130256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-130256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I 