erator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}))}^{2}+(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={(a\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+2ab\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2} \\\\  & +a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{b}^{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2} \\\\  & +ab\\cdot (2\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is *not* the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a[{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{y}_{1}]+b[{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+b{(\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}),$ the operator $D$ is $\\text{nonlinear}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-337739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f02d4e05e1514d523792d5d9e48497a88d0a14a3d5392cc77fed0b9f3315f7"} {"question" "q-337739" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a44137