rse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-337739" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "nonlinear"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-338094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following differential operator:\n\n$$\nD(y)=y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y\n$$\n\nFill in the steps in the reasoning below.\n\nFor any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={{field-2}}-2\\cdot {{field-3}} \\\\  & +ab\\cdot {{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a[{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{1}]+b[{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since {{field-5}} \nthe operator $D$ is {{field-6}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-338094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For any linear differential operator $L,$ we have the linearity condition\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aL({y}_{1})+bL({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nfor functions ${y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x),$ and where $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nFor the given differential operator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})(a\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x})-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+ab{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+ab{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2a{y}_{1}-2b{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2\\cdot (a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & +ab\\cdot ({y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}) \\\\ .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is *not* the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}) & =a[{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{1}]+b[{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{y}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}x}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}x}-2(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $D(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\ne aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2}),$ the operator $D$ is $\\text{nonlinear}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1726288a19a32e552318d2a441375affcd1c6eabb6d29d8733236104e595980"} {"question" "q-338094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072388/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "10f02d4e05e1514d523792d5d9e48497a88d0a14a3d5392cc77fed0b9f3315f7"} {"question" "q-338094" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/ho